      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Dr. Anneliese Voss ran the Tamsin Valley Clinic for the loggers and the Corvane mine crews. In February the miners started coming in with a cough that would not clear, and by March their chest films were white. Voss wrote to the County, then to the State. Cordon Medical answered: they chained her front doors, papered them with a quarantine notice, turned the waiting room into a screening line and moved the sick upstairs into an isolation ward, restrained and sedated with her own narcotics. On the night of the Hum the ward woke up. Nurse Marta Reyes went up with the syringes and the drug-closet key and never came down; Cordon Medical's people bolted the ambulance door behind them and left. Voss shut herself in with her records. Patient 1's films, a week apart, are still on the lightbox in x-ray.",
